{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the two ends</b> of <b>the two twisted cords</b> — the two ends of each one." "<b>You shall put on the two settings.</b> These are the very settings mentioned above, between the section of the breastpiece and the section of the ephod; he did not specify their function and location. Now he explains that the ends of the twisted cords inserted into the rings of the breastpiece are to be fastened in them, on the right and on the left near the neck. The two ends of the right chain he fastens in the settings on the right, and likewise on the left — the two ends of the left chain." "<b>And you shall put.</b> the settings" "<b>on the shoulder-pieces of the ephod</b> — one on this one and one on that one. So the shoulder-pieces of the ephod support the breastpiece so it does not fall, and on them it hangs. Yet the lower edge of the breastpiece comes and rests against his abdomen and is not properly attached to it — therefore two more rings were still needed below it, as he goes on to explain." "<b>Toward its front.</b> Of the ephod — that he should not place the settings on the side of the shoulder-pieces facing the robe, but on the upper side facing outward. And that is called 'in front of the ephod,' for that side which is not visible is not called 'front.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:17.390083574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}